#: ../../api/qfeval_functions.functions.signif.rst:2
msgid "signif"
msgstr ""

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:1
msgid ""
"Rounds the numbers of the given tensor to the specified number of "
"significant digits."
msgstr "指定されたテンソルの数値を、指定された有効桁数に丸めます。"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:4
msgid ""
"Unlike :func:`torch.round`, which rounds to a fixed number of decimal "
"places, this function keeps the given number of significant digits, so "
"the rounding precision adapts to the magnitude of each element (e.g., "
"rounding to 3 significant digits maps 12345 to 12300 and 0.012345 to "
"0.0123).  This is the same behavior as R's ``signif`` function, and the "
"default number of digits follows it.  Zeros and non-finite values (NaN "
"and infinities) are returned unchanged."
msgstr "小数点以下の固定桁数に丸める :func:`torch.round` と異なり、この関数は指定された有効桁数を保つため、丸めの精度は各要素の大きさに応じて変化します（例: 有効数字 3 桁への丸めでは、12345 は 12300 に、0.012345 は 0.0123 になります）。これは R の ``signif`` 関数と同じ動作であり、デフォルトの桁数もそれに従います。ゼロおよび有限でない値（NaN と無限大）はそのまま返されます。"

#: ../../api/qfeval_functions.functions.signif.rst
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "パラメータ"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:13
msgid "The input tensor."
msgstr "入力テンソル。"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:16
msgid ""
"The number of significant digits to keep.  Default is 6, the same default"
" as R's ``signif`` function."
msgstr "保持する有効桁数。デフォルトは R の ``signif`` 関数と同じく 6 です。"

#: ../../api/qfeval_functions.functions.signif.rst
msgid "Returns"
msgstr "戻り値"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:20
msgid ""
"A tensor of the same shape as the input, with each element rounded to the"
" specified number of significant digits."
msgstr "各要素が指定された有効桁数に丸められた、入力と同じ形状のテンソル。"

#: ../../api/qfeval_functions.functions.signif.rst
msgid "Return type"
msgstr "戻り値の型"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:25
msgid "Example"
msgstr "使用例"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:27
msgid ""
">>> x = torch.tensor([3.14159265, 2.71828183])\n"
">>> QF.signif(x, 3)\n"
"tensor([3.1400, 2.7200])"
msgstr ">>> x = torch.tensor([3.14159265, 2.71828183])\n>>> QF.signif(x, 3)\ntensor([3.1400, 2.7200])"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:31
msgid ""
">>> # Zeros are kept as is, and the magnitude adapts per element.\n"
">>> x = torch.tensor([0.0, 100.0])\n"
">>> QF.signif(x, 3)\n"
"tensor([  0., 100.])"
msgstr ">>> # ゼロはそのまま保持され、桁の大きさは要素ごとに適応します。\n>>> x = torch.tensor([0.0, 100.0])\n>>> QF.signif(x, 3)\ntensor([  0., 100.])"

#: of qfeval_functions.functions.signif.signif:36
msgid ""
"``torch.round``: Rounds to a number of decimal places instead of "
"significant digits."
msgstr "``torch.round``: 有効数字ではなく小数点以下の桁数で丸めます。"

